1. What is the difference between Git Merge and Git Rebase?

   1. Git Merge combines changes from one branch into another and creates a merge commit when required.
   2. Git Rebase moves our commits on top of another branch, creating a linear commit history.
   3. Merge preserves the original branch history, whereas rebase rewrites commit history.
   4. I prefer merge for shared branches and rebase to keep my local feature branch updated with the latest changes.

