19. How would you design consistent error responses across 20 endpoints?

   1. I would create a common error response DTO containing timestamp, status, error code, message, path and correlation ID.
   2. I would implement @RestControllerAdvice with @ExceptionHandler methods.
   3. I would define custom exceptions for validation, resource not found, business errors and unexpected failures.
   4. All controllers would use the same response structure, making error handling consistent for frontend applications.

   Example:

   public class ErrorResponse {
       private LocalDateTime timestamp;
       private int status;
       private String errorCode;
       private String message;
       private String path;
       private String traceId;
   }

   Global handler:

   @RestControllerAdvice
   public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

       @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
       public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleNotFound(
               ResourceNotFoundException ex) {

           // Build a standard error response.
           ErrorResponse response = new ErrorResponse();

           // Return HTTP 404.
           return ResponseEntity
                   .status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
                   .body(response);
       }
   }

